SodaDEX limit settlement: original project implementation, MIT.

Permit2 function/struct signatures and EIP-712 witness protocol follow
Uniswap/permit2 (MIT), source commit cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219:
https://github.com/Uniswap/permit2/tree/cc56ad0f3439c502c246fc5cfcc3db92bb8b7219

Canonical Router command/action layout follows the already-deployed
Universal Router 2.1.2 source pinned by this repository:
https://github.com/Uniswap/universal-router/tree/802fe4c18f47300e0f183e2a42e9146ec2ea9fc3

The LimitOrderReactor/LimitOrderLib design was reviewed as a reference for
Permit2 witness settlement. No reactor implementation is copied or deployed;
the reference itself retains GPL-2.0-or-later:
https://github.com/Uniswap/UniswapX/blob/main/src/reactors/LimitOrderReactor.sol
https://github.com/Uniswap/UniswapX/blob/main/src/lib/LimitOrderLib.sol

Tests obtain canonical Permit2 runtime from the user's owned local rehearsal
snapshot. Build tooling records its SHA-256 and does not edit its bytecode.
Forge-std/ds-test are local test dependencies retaining their own licenses;
they are not part of the settlement production compilation.
